WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.188 --> 00:00:22.251
Tennis camp didn't get any easier as the week wore on.

2
00:00:22.252 --> 00:00:31.156
After days of hitting the ball to herself against the practice wall, Iris paired up with Javier on Friday.

3
00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:39.155
The two of them had improved but just barely. Iris felt like a dismal failure at tennis so far.

4
00:00:39.156 --> 00:00:44.875
At least it's Friday, she told herself. The last day of being grounded.

5
00:00:44.876 --> 00:00:50.407
Tomorrow she could finally get back to the park and play soccer with her friends.

6
00:00:50.407 --> 00:00:59.094
Just then Javier launched the ball to Iris, snapping her out of her thoughts. Without thinking, she swung.

7
00:00:59.096 --> 00:01:05.629
And missed. Iris groaned.

8
00:01:05.629 --> 00:01:15.288
"Iris!" Ally appeared behind her. "What's going on, girlfriend? That is not how I taught you to swing."

9
00:01:15.289 --> 00:01:20.127
"I was thinking about soccer," Iris admitted.

10
00:01:20.128 --> 00:01:25.190
"Soccer." Javier rolled his eyes from across the net.

11
00:01:25.192 --> 00:01:29.145
"When you play tennis, you have to think about tennis.

12
00:01:29.145 --> 00:01:35.704
The same goes for you." Ally pointed at Javier. "Let me see you two practice again."

13
00:01:35.705 --> 00:01:45.019
Iris pulled her racket back, tossed the ball in the air, and swung. The ball sailed through the air to Javier.

14
00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:55.007
Javier hit it back. Iris focused. She watched the ball, holding her racket steady as Ally had shown her.

15
00:01:55.008 --> 00:02:02.658
She swung, and with a delicate ping, her racket sent the ball flying back to Javier again.

16
00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:05.526
He returned it to her.

17
00:02:05.527 --> 00:02:08.179
It was a miracle!

18
00:02:08.179 --> 00:02:15.907
"Much better!" Ally said. "Now that you've got the basics down, I think you're ready to play some practice matches.

19
00:02:15.908 --> 00:02:25.894
Anna and Risa are ready too. They are our other beginners." She pointed at a couple of skinny girls clumsily clutching their rackets.

20
00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:33.737
"All right, everyone!" Ally called. "Gather around, and I'll give you an overview of the game rules."

21
00:02:33.738 --> 00:02:42.960
Everyone sat cross-legged on the court in front of Ally. "The main goal is to score points by hitting the ball to your opponent's side of the court.

22
00:02:42.961 --> 00:02:46.973
Actually, Ben and Grace, can you demonstrate?"

23
00:02:46.974 --> 00:02:56.308
"Sure!" Grace and Ben jumped up and jogged to opposite sides of the net.

24
00:02:56.309 --> 00:03:04.739
Grace effortlessly hit the ball to Ben's court—far from Ben.

25
00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.326
He wasn't able to hit it back.

26
00:03:07.327 --> 00:03:10.466
"Fifteen–love!" Ally called.

27
00:03:10.466 --> 00:03:18.872
One of the skinny girls laughed. "Why did you just say 'love'? They're not in love—they're brother and sister!"

28
00:03:18.873 --> 00:03:21.107
Iris was confused too.

29
00:03:21.108 --> 00:03:25.848
"The point system in tennis is a little weird," Ally said.

30
00:03:25.848 --> 00:03:36.946
"You need four points to win, but instead of counting from one to four, the count is fifteen, thirty, forty, and game."

31
00:03:36.947 --> 00:03:46.909
She grinned. "Love means zero points. And we announce the points on both sides, always starting with the person who served.

32
00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:54.236
Since Grace served and made a point, her score is fifteen, and Ben's score is love."

33
00:03:54.237 --> 00:04:02.251
"Everything about this sport is frustrating," Iris thought. "In soccer when you score one goal, you score one point.

34
00:04:02.252 --> 00:04:05.705
Why does tennis scoring have to be so complicated?"

35
00:04:05.706 --> 00:04:10.818
"Grace is the server for this game, so she'll serve again," Ally said.

36
00:04:10.818 --> 00:04:14.966
Grace slammed the ball across the court.

37
00:04:14.967 --> 00:04:20.550
This time Ben bounded toward it and hit the ball back to her.

38
00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:32.230
Back and forth, back and forth it went, until Ben finally sent the ball beyond Grace's reach.

39
00:04:32.231 --> 00:04:40.141
"Fifteen all!" Ally called. She waved for Ben and Grace to return to the group.

40
00:04:40.142 --> 00:04:49.119
"Grace and Ben have been playing a game," Ally went on, "which goes until one player makes four points.

41
00:04:49.120 --> 00:05:02.014
A set is a group of games that goes until one player wins six games, and then a match goes until one player wins two or three sets."

42
00:05:02.015 --> 00:05:06.734
"Game, set, match!" Grace and Ben chanted.

43
00:05:06.735 --> 00:05:10.867
"That sounds exhausting," Iris muttered.

44
00:05:10.867 --> 00:05:16.070
"It's exciting!" Ben said. "Especially when the score is even."

45
00:05:16.071 --> 00:05:22.856
"Exactly," Ally said. "After lunch you can all play doubles games. It'll be fun."

46
00:05:22.856 --> 00:05:30.592
Ally started calling out the partners for doubles. "Iris and Javier, you can play against Anna and Risa."

47
00:05:30.593 --> 00:05:34.296
Ally nodded at the other two newbies in the younger group.

48
00:05:34.297 --> 00:05:37.418
Iris couldn't help feeling relieved.

49
00:05:37.418 --> 00:05:43.735
At least she and Javier had a chance of winning against the skinny younger girls!

50
00:05:43.736 --> 00:05:47.916
The twins' chance for winning evaporated almost immediately.

51
00:05:47.917 --> 00:05:55.306
Anna already had a powerful serve, and Risa was quick to dive to any spot on her part of the court.

52
00:05:55.306 --> 00:06:03.958
They didn't hit the ball every time, but between the two of them, the girls managed to mount the score to forty–love.

53
00:06:03.959 --> 00:06:07.443
"Go, Anna!" a voice called.

54
00:06:07.444 --> 00:06:18.062
A group of the older kids had gathered to watch them play, and Iris' heart sank when she saw it was Zoe cheering on the other team.

55
00:06:18.062 --> 00:06:21.891
"Anna is Zoe's little sister," someone said.

56
00:06:21.892 --> 00:06:27.365
Iris saw Jae standing at Zoe's side, where he'd spent most of the week.

57
00:06:27.366 --> 00:06:33.609
But when Iris caught his gaze, he smiled and gave her an encouraging nod.

58
00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:39.457
"I think he's rooting for me!" Iris thought. She dug deeper.

59
00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:46.513
If she had to do battle against these little girls with Jae watching, she wanted to show her best effort.

60
00:06:46.514 --> 00:06:57.349
The next time Anna served the ball, Iris launched herself forward and batted it back across the net.

61
00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:00.100
"Good one!" Ally said.

62
00:07:00.101 --> 00:07:03.445
"Yeah, Iris!" someone yelled.

63
00:07:03.445 --> 00:07:15.350
Iris realized it was Jae and grinned stupidly. She didn't see the ball coming at her until it was too late.

64
00:07:15.351 --> 00:07:18.687
Miss.

65
00:07:18.688 --> 00:07:23.163
"Game, Anna and Risa!" Ally announced.

66
00:07:23.163 --> 00:07:31.742
The younger girls raised their rackets in the air, and the crowd cheered—even Jae.

67
00:07:31.742 --> 00:07:38.911
"Wait!" Iris protested. "I wasn't ready for that last serve!"

68
00:07:38.911 --> 00:07:47.394
"Iris!" Javier hissed loudly, and everyone looked over at them. His cheeks were bright red.

69
00:07:47.395 --> 00:07:57.396
"Drop it, will you?" He shot a quick look at Jae. "This isn't a big competition or anything. You're embarrassing us."

70
00:07:57.397 --> 00:08:07.223
Iris swallowed hard, her own cheeks flushing with heat. "I'm not the one embarrassing us!" she snapped. "I just—"

71
00:08:07.224 --> 00:08:14.708
Ally cut in before Iris could finish. "Great game, everyone! Next group, you're up!"

72
00:08:14.709 --> 00:08:21.193
Iris slinked off the court, Javier at her heels.

73
00:08:21.194 --> 00:08:31.601
She knew she'd acted like a sore loser, but Javier had made it worse by embarrassing her in front of everyone, especially Jae.

74
00:08:31.601 --> 00:08:37.678
"You need to chill," Javier muttered. "It's just a game."

75
00:08:37.679 --> 00:08:45.757
"I get it." Iris glared at him. "Although I think the person who needs a chill pill right now is you."

76
00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:53.099
"Whatever." Javier shook his head like he felt sorry for her. "You're acting like such a baby.

77
00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:55.975
I don't want to be your doubles partner anymore."

78
00:08:55.976 --> 00:08:59.573
"Fine by me!" Iris snapped.

79
00:08:59.573 --> 00:09:15.012
She couldn't be on the same doubles team as her brother anyway since, as of that moment, she was no longer speaking to him.
